    "description": "Ishida model AC-4000D self-indicating, price-computing, multi-interval electronic non-automatic weighing instrument. Intended for pre-packaging use and not intended for trading direct with the public (notice provided). Fitted with an integral label printer. Capabilities for tare and preset-tare (including pre-set tare values associated with product look-up tables), initial and semi-automatic zero setting devices and a zero-tracking device. Composed of three separate modules: basework/platform, printer unit (contains the main board of the instrument, including the A/D board) and display/keyboard. RS-232 and Ethernet interfacing capabilities available; only the Ethernet option was installed on the sample instrument. Powered by mains supply. Load receptor nominal dimensions 400 mm x 254 mm; the sample was provided with a level bubble beneath the platter, with a window in the platter required so the bubble could be seen without removing the load receptor."
